    "Adjust forecasts downward when sentiment history shows sustained negative sentiment (e.g., multiple -0.25 or 0.00 values) indicating market pessimism.",
    "Increase forecast sensitivity to recent price spikes — if true outcome exceeds model forecast by >5% and sentiment is neutral or positive, apply a 10-15% upward correction to next period.",
    "Apply mean reversion bias: if model consistently overpredicts prices in early periods (e.g., first 5-7 days of history), reduce forecast by 2-5% for subsequent days.",
    "Correct for lagged overreaction: if model forecasts spike after a recent high, reduce forecast by 5-10% to account for market cooling.",
    "When sentiment shifts from negative to positive (e.g., 0.00 → 0.50 or 0.67), increase forecast by 3-7% to reflect potential momentum.",
    "Avoid overfitting to recent history: if model forecasts are overly influenced by last 3-5 days (e.g., 70.93, 70.91, 70.18), apply a 5-10% downward adjustment to prevent overestimation of short-term volatility."
